warning
# Issue #1494: a recorded prior worker for the issue was still running
# when a replacement rework launch was requested, and was reaped
# (process-tree killed + orphan sweep) before the replacement dispatched.
# Warning, not error: the reap is a recovery — the superseded worker is
# gone and dispatch proceeds. The sibling ``superseded_worker_reap_failed``
# records a pid that survived the reap attempt (or was live with no
# start-time fingerprint) and blocked the replacement launch.
